=> One important thing to remember

.j2 file is NOT the final file.

It is a template.

For example:

test.j2

contains:

My hostname is {{ ansible_facts['hostname'] }}

After Ansible processes it, the target gets:

/tmp/hostname

containing:

My hostname is ip-172-31-5-139

=> Flow:-

                 WSL
          Ansible Control Node
                  |
                  |
        templates/test.j2
                  |
                  |
                  ↓
     My hostname is
     {{ ansible_facts['hostname'] }}
                  |
                  | Ansible processes Jinja2
                  ↓
            Target Server
                  |
                  ↓
          /tmp/hostname
                  |
                  ↓
     My hostname is
     ip-172-31-5-139

Also it will create the final file at /tmp/hostname on the target server.

This is important.

src → Control Node

dest → Target Server

